# ⏱️ 1. Execution Time Decorator

A decorator can measure how long a function takes to execute.

### Logic

```text
Start Time
    ↓
Run Function
    ↓
End Time
    ↓
Execution Time = End Time - Start Time
```

### Main Pattern

```python
start = time.time()

result = function(*args, **kwargs)

end = time.time()

print("Execution Time:", end - start)

return result
```

---

# 💻 Practice 1 — Task Execution Time

```python
import time

def decorator(function):

    def wrapper(*args, **kwargs):

        start = time.time()

        result = function(*args, **kwargs)

        end = time.time()

        print("Execution Time:", end - start)

        return result

    return wrapper


@decorator
def task():

    time.sleep(2)

    print("Task Completed")


task()
```

